Package: rcontext
Title: Make Your Live R Session Visible to Terminal Coding Agents
Version: 0.1.2
Authors@R:
    person("Yuya", "Ogawa", , "yuya19991230@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Terminal coding agents such as Claude Code and GitHub Copilot
    CLI run in a separate process from R, so they cannot see the objects you
    have loaded, the commands you have run, or the errors those commands
    threw. This package exposes that session state to them over the Model
    Context Protocol, so they can read your environment and console instead
    of guessing from source files. A single setup() call registers the
    server with every agent it finds and arranges for future R sessions to
    announce themselves automatically.
